# Frequency Domain Analysis

This chapter introduces the **frequency domain** representation of signals and explains the fundamental mathematical tools used in Digital Signal Processing (DSP).

---

## 📘 Topics Covered

### 1️⃣ Fourier Series
- Representation of periodic signals as a sum of sinusoids
- Decomposes a periodic signal into harmonic components
- Useful for analyzing periodic waveforms

---

### 2️⃣ Fourier Transform (FT)
- Converts a time-domain signal into its frequency-domain representation
- Applicable to non-periodic signals
- Reveals frequency content of signals

---

### 3️⃣ Fourier Transform Properties
- Linearity  
- Time shifting  
- Frequency shifting  
- Convolution property  
- Parseval’s theorem  

These properties simplify signal analysis and system design.

---
### 4️⃣ Fast Fourier Transform (FFT)

- Efficient algorithm to compute the Discrete Fourier Transform (DFT)
- Reduces computational complexity from:

    O(N^2)  →  O(N log N)

- Makes real-time DSP systems possible

---

### 5️⃣ Windowing
- Used before FFT to reduce spectral leakage
- Common window functions:
  - Hamming
  - Hanning
  - Blackman
  - Rectangular

---

### 6️⃣ Spectrogram
- Time-frequency representation of a signal
- Shows how frequency content changes over time
- Useful for:
  - Speech analysis
  - Radar signal analysis
  - Communication signals

---
