# Fourier Series

The basics of the frequency domain start with understanding that **any signal can be represented as a sum of sine waves**.

When we break a signal down into its composite sine waves, this representation is called a **Fourier Series**.

In simple terms:

> A complex signal = sum of simple sine and cosine waves.

